BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  Long ago, in the Realm of Echoes, lived two spirits: Aethel, the Weaver of Light, and Thorne, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    the Keeper of Stones. They resided on separate peaks, divided by an abyss of starlight. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    Great Creator decreed that they could only transcend their isolation by sharing their gifts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (     Each day, Aethel cast strands of golden silk across the void, trusting Thorne to catch them) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    . If Thorne caught the silk and wove it into a bridge, the return was grand-a harvest of sta) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    rdust that nourished them both. Yet, if Thorne greedily hoarded the silk, the bridge would c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    ollapse, and both would languish in darkness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  One cycle, Aethel sent everything she had, a bold act of faith. Thorne, standing at the precip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (    ice, felt the weight of the gift. He chose not to keep the silk for himself, but to weave it) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (     into a path of shimmering quartz. When the bridge solidified, the void vanished, and the tw) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    o became one, their combined light illuminating the entire cosmos. They learned that the aby) Tj ET
