BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (Assistant output:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  In the Realm of Echoes, the Weaver and the Keeper held the balance of existence in their hands) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    . The Weaver began each cycle with five golden fibers-the essence of potential. To create, t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    he Weaver had to entrust these fibers to the Keeper. Upon the Keeper's threshold, the fibers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (     tripled in brilliance, becoming a shimmering cascade of raw light.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  The Keeper faced the ultimate choice: to hoard the gold or to weave it into a tapestry of trus) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    t. If the Keeper clutched the treasure tightly, the light faded, becoming cold, unmoving met) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    al. But if the Keeper returned a generous portion, the threads fused into a bridge, connecti) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ng their separate worlds. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  They soon learned that the cycle was not about the gold itself, but the act of passing it betw) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    een hands. When the Weaver gave with open palms and the Keeper returned with an honest heart) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    , the light grew until it illuminated the stars. Greed was a wall that kept both in the shad) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    ows, while reciprocity was the loom upon which their shared destiny was woven. Thus, they de) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    creed: he who gives, receives, and he who nurtures the gift finds that the value of the thre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    ad is surpassed only by the bond forged in the exchange.) Tj ET
