BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    elestial bazaar. He stood before the Weaver of Threads, a deity who could triple whatever wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    s cast into her loom. The Merchant knew that keeping the seeds would yield only a modest har) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    vest of wheat. Yet, he feared the abyss of the Weaver's silence. If he placed his seeds upon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (     her altar, would she return the bounty, or keep the gold for her own gilded halls?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  Summoning courage, the Merchant placed all five seeds into the void. The loom whirred, the mag) Tj ET
