BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  In the beginning, the world was barren, held in the static grip of isolation. Solis, the spiri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    t of Abundance, possessed five golden embers, the seeds of potential. Luna, the spirit of Gr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    owth, stood across the chasm of the void. Solis knew that embers alone were cold; they requi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    red the fertile soil of Luna's garden.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  With a leap of faith, Solis cast three embers across the divide. Luna caught them, her hands g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    lowing with the warmth of the gift. She did not hoard them in her dark pockets. Instead, she) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (     planted them in the loam of her spirit, where they bloomed into a magnificent tree of light) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    , its branches heavy with golden fruit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  Recognizing the origin of the harvest, Luna gathered the bounty and cast back a portion to Sol) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    is. The cycle pulsed, vibrating with the rhythm of reciprocity. Had Solis been stingy, the e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    mbers would have faded into ash. Had Luna been greedy, the garden would have withered in sha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    dow. But through the bridge of trust, they turned five embers into a forest of prosperity. T) Tj ET
