BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  In the beginning, there was only the Void, silent and stagnant. Then, the Weaver and the Harve) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    ster met at the edge of existence. The Weaver held a single golden thread, a gift from the s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    tars. She faced a choice: she could keep it, clutching its warmth in the freezing dark, or s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    he could cast it into the abyss, trusting the Harvester to catch it. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  She cast it forth, and the thread tripled in length, glowing with infinite potential as it tra) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    veled through the void. The Harvester, seeing the beauty of the gift, did not hoard the boun) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    ty. He wove the thread back, returning a portion to the Weaver, ensuring the cycle of creati) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    on continued. They realized that when one hoards, the thread remains a mere string, but when) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (     one shares, it becomes a tapestry that spans the cosmos. The secret of the gods was simple:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (     the value of a token is not in its possession, but in its circulation. To keep is to remain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (     in shadow; to give is to invite the light of growth. They built a bridge of golden threads,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (     a testament to the balance between risk and reward. In the dance of the Weaver and the Harv) Tj ET
