BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      In the beginning, the Weaver and the Wanderer stood on opposite sides of the Great Chasm. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        The Weaver held five glimmering shards of light. The Weaver knew that if these shards we) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        re held tight, they would surely dim. If offered to the Wanderer across the void, howeve) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        r, the magic of the chasm would triple their brilliance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      The Weaver extended a hand, casting all five shards into the dark. The Wanderer caught the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (         glowing treasure, now fifteen shards strong. The Wanderer faced a choice: keep the ligh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        t to illuminate only their own path, or return a portion to the Weaver, honoring the cou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        rage of the gift. Recognizing that the Weaver had risked everything, the Wanderer sent a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (         generous portion back, ensuring that both could walk the bridge safely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      From that day, the inhabitants of the stars learned the law of the Chasm: abundance is nev) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        er found in hoarding. When the Weaver trusts the Wanderer, and the Wanderer honors the W) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        eaver, the light multiplies, and the bridge holds firm. To hold on is to lose, but to gi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        ve is to invite a return that sustains the harmony of the universe. Trust is the gravity) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (         that binds the cosmos together.) Tj ET
