BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        their gifts. Each day, Aethel cast strands of golden silk across the void, trusting Thor) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        ne to catch them. If Thorne caught the silk and wove it into a bridge, the return was gr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        and-a harvest of stardust that nourished them both. Yet, if Thorne greedily hoarded the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        silk, the bridge would collapse, and both would languish in darkness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
