BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      In the Realm of Echoes, the Weaver and the Keeper held the balance of existence in their h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        ands. The Weaver began each cycle with five golden fibers-the essence of potential. To c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        reate, the Weaver had to entrust these fibers to the Keeper. Upon the Keeper's threshold) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        , the fibers tripled in brilliance, becoming a shimmering cascade of raw light.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      The Keeper faced the ultimate choice: to hoard the gold or to weave it into a tapestry of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        trust. If the Keeper clutched the treasure tightly, the light faded, becoming cold, unmo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        ving metal. But if the Keeper returned a generous portion, the threads fused into a brid) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        ge, connecting their separate worlds. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      They soon learned that the cycle was not about the gold itself, but the act of passing it ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        between hands. When the Weaver gave with open palms and the Keeper returned with an hone) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        st heart, the light grew until it illuminated the stars. Greed was a wall that kept both) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (         in the shadows, while reciprocity was the loom upon which their shared destiny was wove) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        n. Thus, they decreed: he who gives, receives, and he who nurtures the gift finds that t) Tj ET
