BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        . The Miller, standing at the millstone, understands this grain is a testament to the Ha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        rvester's courage. To hoard the flour is to halt the river, but to share it is to keep t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        he waters flowing, nourishing both parties. This cycle is the marrow of their bond, a te) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        stament to the belief that prosperity is not a finite resource to be guarded, but an ene) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        rgy to be circulated. Each time the Harvester offers all, and the Miller returns a gener) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        ous portion, they are planting seeds for future cycles. They have learned that the riche) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (        st harvest is not the grain itself, but the enduring trust that makes the flow possible.) Tj ET
