BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      ished, a lonely thread in a sea of gray. But to cast the strand into the Loom of Reciproci) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      ty is to watch it multiply into a triad of shimmering silk. The second weaver, standing at) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (       the frame, holds the shuttle of fate. They must decide whether to knot the thread in self) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      ishness or to weave it into a pattern that binds both travelers together. If the shuttle r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      emains still, the design unravels into chaos, leaving the loom cold and barren. But when t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      he weaver catches the triple threads and weaves them back into the fabric, a masterpiece e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      merges, vibrant and strong. This exchange is the rhythm of existence-a dance of release an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      d retrieval. We learn that no single hand can craft the tapestry alone; the beauty of the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      design depends entirely on the willingness to entrust our golden thread to another. By ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      urning the silk, the weaver ensures the loom continues to spin, proving that trust is the ) Tj ET
